WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.150
Here are the best drugstore
products I tested in 2022.

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:05.640
Let's start with face products.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.706
The ELF Power Grip primer creates

00:00:07.706 --> 00:00:10.089
a really nice tacky base for foundation

00:00:10.089 --> 00:00:12.420
that's meant to make
your makeup last longer.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.270
My foundation blended out
really nicely on top of this,

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:17.730
and I do think my makeup
lasted really well,

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.710
even my blush, which is literally always

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.600
the first thing to disappear on my face.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.690
The ELF Halo Glow Liquid
Filter is a great dupe

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.060
for the Charlotte Tilbury Flawless Filter.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.651
It gives you a really glowy

00:00:28.651 --> 00:00:30.442
your-skin-but-better base.

00:00:30.442 --> 00:00:32.804
These Versed Mood Lighting
Luminizing Glow Drops

00:00:32.804 --> 00:00:34.110
are a similar product.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.210
They do give a beautiful glow to the skin,

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.220
but they don't really have any coverage.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.320
They do have a lot of
great skincare ingredients

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.260
that made my skin feel
really nice and hydrated.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.330
This ELF luminous putty bronzer goes

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.850
from this putty formula to a powder.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.860
Up close, you can see a
lot of shimmer in this,

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.960
but it doesn't look that way on the skin.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.018
This is one of the most blendable bronzers

00:00:54.018 --> 00:00:55.426
I've ever tried, and it brings

00:00:55.426 --> 00:00:57.990
a really natural warmth to the skin.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:00:59.850
Milani's Conceal + Perfect contour

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.500
and highlighter are really good.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.150
These kind of feel like
a drugstore version

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.010
of the Charlotte Tilbury wands.

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.930
The contour blended
out really beautifully,

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:08.520
and the highlighter gave a pretty glow

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.350
without emphasizing my texture.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:11.880
The ELF Halo Glow powder puff

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:14.271
has become a staple product for me.

00:01:14.271 --> 00:01:15.750
It does pick up a lot of product,

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:17.490
but this sets makeup so beautifully,

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.110
and it's such great quality.

00:01:19.110 --> 00:01:21.120
Like, you wouldn't think this is $4.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.195
The Jason Wu Beauty blush trio

00:01:23.195 --> 00:01:25.086
is more on the pricey
side of the drugstore,

00:01:25.086 --> 00:01:26.735
but I think it's so worth it.

00:01:26.735 --> 00:01:28.740
The blushes all blend out so easily

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.720
and look so smooth on the skin.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.915
The color payoff on these is also great.

00:01:32.915 --> 00:01:34.223
Moving on to eye products,

00:01:34.223 --> 00:01:36.503
this Jason Wu Beauty Flora 4 palette

00:01:36.503 --> 00:01:39.600
was surprisingly pigmented
and easy to blend.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.700
Also, this jewel stick was incredible.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.920
Look how much it brightened
up my inner corners.

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:45.810
The ELF Lash 'N Roll mascara

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.970
really coats every single lash.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:49.203
My lashes are so straight,

00:01:49.203 --> 00:01:50.661
but this gave them a nice curl.

00:01:50.661 --> 00:01:53.250
I wish it thickened my
lashes more, but for 6 bucks,

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:55.650
this is a really good drugstore mascara.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:59.490
These NYX Jumbo Lash lashes
are so easy to apply,

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:01.590
and the band is really comfortable.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:03.427
I think these have totally convinced me

00:02:03.427 --> 00:02:04.860
to wear lashes more often.

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.747
The NYX Thick It Stick It brow gel

00:02:06.747 --> 00:02:08.550
is a thickening brow mascara.

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.235
If you look really close, you can see

00:02:10.235 --> 00:02:12.060
those little fibers that are supposed to

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:13.513
make your brows look fluffier.

00:02:13.513 --> 00:02:16.248
I really like the natural full-brow effect

00:02:16.248 --> 00:02:17.423
you get with this.

00:02:17.423 --> 00:02:19.320
Next, let's talk about lip products.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.570
This is the Maybelline
Super Stay Vinyl Ink

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.120
Longwear No-Budge liquid lipcolor.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.428
This is a long-wearing lipstick

00:02:25.428 --> 00:02:26.786
that's meant to stay shiny.

00:02:26.786 --> 00:02:29.640
You have to shake it for
five seconds, then apply.

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:31.410
Even though I did get a little transfer

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:33.395
and the shine isn't
long-lasting, the lipstick

00:02:33.395 --> 00:02:36.000
itself stays super
bright and doesn't budge.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.277
These are the L'Oréal
Colour Riche Intense Volume

00:02:38.277 --> 00:02:39.420
matte lipsticks.

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:41.677
The color payoff on these is so good,

00:02:41.677 --> 00:02:43.710
and they apply really smoothly.

00:02:43.710 --> 00:02:45.870
This is one of the most
comfortable matte formulas

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:48.330
I've ever tried, especially
from the drugstore.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.187
The Jason Wu Extra Pout lip plumper

00:02:50.187 --> 00:02:52.628
is a holy-grail product for me.

00:02:52.628 --> 00:02:55.050
Even if you don't care about
the lip-pluming aspect,

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.270
this is one of the best lip-gloss formulas

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:58.650
I've ever tried.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.440
It's so cushiony and shiny and amazing,

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:02.850
and everyone should get it.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:04.720
This ELF Cookies 'n Dreams lip gloss

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.960
in Cookie Dreams is a black
lip gloss with a bunch

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:09.270
of pretty blue and silver
glitter throughout.

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:11.430
On its own, it gives a bluish-black tint.

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:13.350
I love it more over other lip products.

00:03:13.350 --> 00:03:15.314
It's really good for deepening colors,

00:03:15.314 --> 00:03:16.908
and the formula of the gloss itself

00:03:16.908 --> 00:03:19.410
is actually really nice
for the $4 price point.

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:21.240
I only tested one hair product this year,

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:24.180
and that was the Eco
Styler Unicorn Glitter Gel.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.650
It's a translucent pink color

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:27.540
with blue iridescent sparkles.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.740
Running this through my hair,

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:30.660
you don't really get the glittery effect.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:32.667
You can see the glitter and color better

00:03:32.667 --> 00:03:35.250
when I apply it to
brushed-back straight hair.

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:37.201
This is so cute for a
little glitter moment

00:03:37.201 --> 00:03:38.176
every once in a while,

00:03:38.176 --> 00:03:40.377
and it actually washed
out of my hair easily.

